<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · song</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battōtai</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">words <a href="/years/1882">1882</a>; song <a href="/years/1885">1885</a>; Army March-Past <a href="/years/1886">1886</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as 抜刀隊</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battōtai (&quot;Drawn-Sword Unit&quot;) was a squad of police swordsmen formed by the Meiji government in 1877, during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/satsuma-rebellion">Satsuma Rebellion</a>, the uprising led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saigo-takamori">Saigō Takamori</a>. At the Battle of Tabaruzaka the government's <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/conscription">conscript</a> army, mostly commoners who had never learned to fight with the sword, suffered heavy losses in close combat with Saigō's <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samurai">samurai</a>.</p></div>
